From 5a2385e86ecf65734eb7b531a974dfb3f619d612 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Derek J. Clark" <derekjohn.clark@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:24:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix: Stop and remove source drivers when their device is
 removed

When a source device is removed, on_source_device_removed() cleans up hide
rules, ffb effect registrations capabilities, and source_devices_used, but
never stops the SourceDriver task or removes it from source_devices.
This produces some issues:
- Sources that open their device in blocking/exclusive mode never receive
  a read error when the device is unbound and the poll loop sits in read()
  forever.
- Since the udev-driven removal path is the only one firing for those
  sources and it never calls stop(), every unbind leaks a running task
  and an open fd on the device.
- For a normal evdev unbind both SourceDeviceStopped and
  SourceDeviceRemoved arrive, first with a read-error then from the udev
  remove, and the handler re-runs full cleanup on already-removed state.

To resolve this, make the following changes:
- Add an early return if the device is not in source_devices_used.
- source.stop().await on the remaining driver.
- Remove of the source_devices map entry.

