 src/input/composite_device/mod.rs | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/input/composite_device/mod.rs b/src/input/composite_device/mod.rs
index e23eeb3..4d23a4c 100644
--- a/src/input/composite_device/mod.rs
+++ b/src/input/composite_device/mod.rs
@@ -1290,6 +1290,20 @@ impl CompositeDevice {
         let path = device.path();
         let id = device.get_id();
 
+        // A source task may have already removed this device.
+        if !self.source_devices_used.contains(&id) {
+            log::trace!("Source device {id} was already removed");
+            return Ok(());
+        }
+
+        // Blocked sources never observe their device dying.
+        if let Some(source) = self.source_devices.get(&id) {
+            if let Err(e) = source.stop().await {
+                log::debug!("Failed to stop source device {id}: {e:?}");
+            }
+        }
+        self.source_devices.remove(&id);
+
         // The device node is gone, so drop its hide rules
         if let Some(name) = Path::new(&path).file_name() {
             remove_hide_rules(&name.to_string_lossy());

From 1349d3d5bf20a180632aad259dbc56c63bdd80d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Derek J. Clark" <derekjohn.clark@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:24:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix: Evict userspace clients when hiding devices and
 reannounce on unhide

Since systemd 256, udevadm trigger events no longer unlink or recreate
devnodes, so the remove/add retrigger no longer breaks ioctl for hidden
devices. Because of this, there are some breakages in how device
hide/unhide is handled.
  - Hiding a node no longer evicts userspace clients that already have
    the device open, bypassing the virtual device.
  - Unhiding via the retrigger no longer delivers a real node change, so
    clients holding a hidden node are not prompted to re-open the restored
    one.

Resolve these issues by:
  - After writing the hide rule and reloading rules, rm the devnode and
    recreate it with mkdev as a character device with mode 000.
  - Only do this for ChangePermissions hides as MoveSourceDevice moves the
    node, bypassing the problem.
  - Split the reload plumbing into reload_rules() for a plain rules reload
    and reload_children() for rules reload plus the remove/add trigger.
    hide_device() uses the plain reload to avoid emitting synthetic events
    to our own udev monitor, and unhide_device() keeps the retrigger so
    userspace clients get a fresh add event.
  - Drop the now-unneeded parent lookup from hide_device() and add the
    libc dependency.

