From 182d4ab6c2bc9448049409b6ac8b7a3c0107c78c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Derek J. Clark" <derekjohn.clark@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:24:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] fix: Restore node ownership when unhiding devices

When a device is hidden, SAVED_PERMISSIONS only saves the mode bits.
On unhide the restored node comes back owned by the daemon
(root:root), losing the original ownership such as root:input on
event nodes and breaking group/ACL-based access for non-root clients.

To resolve this, make the following changes:
  - Add a NodeAttributes struct which holds the mode, uid, and gid.
  - Save the uid and gid of the node at hide time.
  - Add restore_node_attributes() which applies the saved mode and
    chown()s the node.
  - Use it in unhide_device() and both restore loops in unhide_all(),
    replacing the inline mode-only blocks.

