From 80d5da8e9557d5a67404524d431d1df7439d2e6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Derek J. Clark" <derekjohn.clark@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:24:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix: monitor input devices via udev instead of inotify

Device discovery runs two inotify watchers over /dev and /dev/input plus
a separate udev monitor for iio only. The inotify path needs a retry loop
to wait for udev initialization and devnode existence before each add is
processed. An inotify remove event means the node was unlinked, not that
the device is gone, which is unreliable for driving removal. Hiding and
unhiding no longer rely on synthetic udev events, so the split
inotify/udev setup adds complexity without adding coverage.

- Replace watch_iio_devices() with watch_udev_devices(), a single udev
  monitor matching the hidraw, iio, and input subsystems.
- Remove the inotify watchers, watch_devnodes(), the DEV_PATH and
  INPUT_PATH constants, src/watcher/, and the inotify dependency.
- Make create_composite_device_from_config() synchronous again and fail
  on ENODEV at open, as that means the device is disconnecting.

